{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpkM1WNeVui6MjvcHatL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Vitest has two ways to do this.\n\n**1. `describe.sequential`**\n\n```ts\nimport { describe, test, expect } from 'vitest'\n\ndescribe.sequential('user flow', () => {\n  test('creates user', async () => { /* ... */ })\n  test('updates user', async () => { /* ... */ })   // starts after \"creates user\" finishes\n  test('deletes user', async () => { /* ... */ })   // starts after \"updates user\" finishes\n})\n```\n\n**2. The `sequential` option (options object as the second argument)**\n\n```ts\ndescribe('user flow', { sequential: true }, () => {\n  test('creates user', async () => { /* ... */ })\n  test('updates user', async () => { /* ... */ })\n})\n```\n\nYou can also set it on a single test with `test.sequential(...)` or `test('name', { sequential: true }, ...)`.\n\n**When you need it:** by default, Vitest already runs the tests inside one file one after another. You only need `sequential` when something has turned on concurrency, for example:\n\n- the suite sits inside a `describe.concurrent` block\n- `sequence: { concurrent: true }` is set in `vitest.config.ts`\n- you run with `--sequence.concurrent`\n\n```ts\ndescribe.concurrent('suite', () => {\n  test('a', async () => {})        // a and b run at the same time\n  test('b', async () => {})\n\n  describe.sequential('ordered', () => {\n    test('c', async () => {})      // c, then d\n    test('d', async () => {})\n  })\n})\n```\n\n**Notes:**\n- This only controls the order of tests inside a file. Separate test files still run in parallel across workers. To run files one at a time, use `--no-file-parallelism` (or `fileParallelism: false` in the config).\n- The options-object form (`{ sequential: true }` as the second argument) is the syntax in current Vitest versions. Older versions accepted options as the third argument, so check your version if you get a type error.\n\nI wrote this from memory. The Ludion knowledge base had nothing on this topic. If something doesn't match, check the API docs for your Vitest version at vitest.dev/api."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":210,"cache_read_input_tokens":4539,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":210},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"658d7039-6a02-4551-910e-ecabba373cd3","uuid":"680c9305-7816-47eb-ad02-8a9a589fe31b","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:11:54.810Z","request_id":"req_011CfpkM1EkVdxctijgyVYoy"}
